From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:18:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: name who a forward is from, whatever it came from

A forwarded message is shown with a line saying who it is from,
"<b>Forwarded from NAME:</b>", in front of its text, a file's file://
URI, the luneos-file: card of a file that waits for a tap, or a poll.
The line was left out when the origin could not be named: a message
forwarded from a group's anonymous admin (messageOriginChat, not
handled at all), or from a channel the account has no chat for, so
such a forward looked like the sender's own words.

Name a group or channel by its title, with the signature of whoever
wrote in it in brackets, as Telegram does: "News (Ann)". A channel not
known is named by the signature alone. With no name at all, say only
that it is forwarded: "<b>Forwarded:</b>".

The Messaging app draws this line as a "Forwarded from" label at the
top of the bubble (app/src/util/forwarded.js), finding it by its exact
form at the start of the text; getForwardHeader documents that form.
Other front-ends show the line as before.

Test in test/webos-commands-test.cpp (WebosTapTest.Forwarded): a
forward from a user, a signed channel, a group, a channel not known,
signed and not, before text, a photo here and photos fetched after the
wait, and a video's card through the tap to its file.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
---
 account-data.h               |   4 +-
 client-utils.cpp             |  21 ++++++-
 identifiers.cpp              |   5 ++
 identifiers.h                |   2 +
 receiving.cpp                |  29 ++++++++--
 test/webos-commands-test.cpp | 104 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 155 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/account-data.h b/account-data.h
index db7b5dc..d8566d8 100644
--- a/account-data.h
+++ b/account-data.h
@@ -153,7 +153,8 @@ struct TgMessageInfo {
     bool        sentLocally = false; // For outgoing messages, whether sent by this very client
     MessageId   repliedMessageId;
     td::td_api::object_ptr<td::td_api::message> repliedMessage;
-    std::string forwardedFrom;
+    std::string forwardedFrom; // who it was forwarded from, if known
+    bool        forwarded = false; // whether it was forwarded, from whoever
     std::string altText; // to show instead of the picture, where it cannot be shown
     bool        anonymousChannelPost = false; // incomingGroupchatSender is "Channel post", naming nobody
     bool        fromHistory = false; // fetched to catch up with a chat, rather than just sent
@@ -174,6 +175,7 @@ struct TgMessageInfo {
         repliedMessageId = other.repliedMessageId;
         repliedMessage = nullptr;
         forwardedFrom = other.forwardedFrom;
+        forwarded = other.forwarded;
